course: dictionary
lesson: 6103
title: Mi: a mile and a musical note
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «mi» is a short way to write mile. A mile is a long unit of length for roads and trips, about 1.6 kilometres. When you see a number before «mi», like «5 mi», read it as five miles.
explain: The same two letters can mean something different in a song. In do, re, mi, mi is the third note of the scale. Look at the words around it: if the text is about distance or speed, it means miles, and if it is about singing or notes, it means a note.
explain: Words also change between places. In Jamaican Patois, «Mi soon come» means I'll be there soon, though maybe later. Here «mi» does not mean mile at all. Context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: «mi» is the short way to write mile.
fact: A mile is about 1.6 kilometres.
fact: «mph» means miles per hour, a speed.
fact: In music, mi is the third note of the scale: do, re, mi.
fact: In Jamaican Patois, «mi» can mean I or my, as in «Wah gwaan, mi baby?» (what's going on, my baby?).
exercise: «The walk to the lake is 3 mi.» What does mi stand for? | metre | minute | *mile | mini
exercise: In singing, do, re, mi. What is mi in that song? | The first note of the scale | *The third note of the scale | The last note of the scale | A loud shout
exercise: Which short form means miles per hour? | kg | mi | km | *mph
test: «The shop is 2 mi away.» About how far is that in kilometres? | About 30 kilometres | About 3 centimetres | About 300 metres | *About 3 kilometres
test: «Mi soon come» is Jamaican Patois. What does it mean? | We are already home | Goodbye forever | *I'll be there soon | Where did you go
exam: Grandma rings from Jamaica and says, «Wah gwaan, mi baby?» What does it mean? | Time for bed now | Where is the bus stop? | *What's going on, my baby? | How many miles is it?
